sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 6, docs/reference/development-containers.md): on an app-dev Node with `settings.apps.containers`, `instance:create` makes a container. The kind and its step names follow docs/cli/instance/create.mmd; the intent carries `runtime: container`. `--from` is drawn in container/copy.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:create
  %% kind: instance.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:create<br/>PROJECT NODE NAME
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:create PROJECT NODE NAME`
  %%> - syntax: `<project> <node> <name> [--root=PATH] [--domain=HOST] [--branch=BRANCH] [--database-server=SLUG] [--from=INSTANCE]`
  %%> Who calls it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI, the MCP tool, and Conn when a thread starts in an Orbit Project
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve Instance<br/>address · T3 port · .env
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has node access to the target Node
  %%> - the target is an active `app-dev` Node with `settings.apps.containers`
  %%> - a database server, when given, is on the same Node, else `instance.database_server_remote` (open question 11 in the plan)
  %%> - no other change runs on the Instance; the Gateway holds one lock per Instance and holds the Route's Nodes
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Instance is reserved with its runtime record: container name, bridge address, a free port from `t3_ports`, and its Route
  %%> - `.env` is rendered from the Project's env template; the placeholder model key and a repository read token go to the vault
  %%> - the intent names the vault key where the run stores the new Gateway session for this T3 server
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent, `runtime: container`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-create
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  opt no current source container for the Project
    SW->>N: Build source container<br/>Ansible · tags source
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - launches `<project>-source-<commit>` from the Node's image, fetches the default branch on the Node with the read token and pushes it in
    %%> - installs the dependencies from the lockfiles as `orbit`, with the install that a cold wake runs today; it runs no setup step, because there is no database and no `.env`
    %%> - stops it; T3 never starts in it, because its unit starts only when `/etc/orbit/instance` exists
    %%> Why:
    %%> - every copy then starts T3 for the first time and makes its own identity
    %%> Once:
    %%> - later creates reuse it; a rebuild makes a new one beside it (open question 8 in the plan)
  end
  SW->>N: Copy source container<br/>Ansible · tags container
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus copy` of the current source container, a ZFS clone
  %%> - sets the bridge address with `security.port_isolation`, so containers on the bridge cannot reach each other
  %%> - sets `limits.cpu`, `limits.memory`, the read-only idmapped mount of `/opt/orbit-agent`, and the T3 proxy device on the Node's WireGuard address and the Instance's port
  %%> - adds the firewall route rule for that port; nothing else of the Node changes
  %%> Branch:
  %%> - fetches the Instance's branch on the Node with the read token, or creates it from the default branch; the token stays on the Node and is removed after the step
  opt database on a Database server
    SW->>N: Create owner and database<br/>child operation-database-create
    %%> What it adds:
    %%> - the same steps as today; the server admits the Node's bridge for this role only
  end
  opt default Instance has a database
    SW->>N: Copy the default database<br/>pg_dump · pg_restore
    %%> Why before setup:
    %%> - the copy lands first, so setup migrates a copy, not an empty database
    %%> How:
    %%> - one consistent `pg_dump` of the default Instance's database while it runs, restored into the new database with `--no-owner --no-privileges`
  end
  SW->>N: Start the container<br/>incus start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - nftables, `hidepid` and the image's units start; T3 does not, because `/etc/orbit/instance` does not exist yet
  SW->>C: Prepare the workspace<br/>Ansible · tags workspace
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - pushes the branch in and checks it out in `/srv/workspace`; sets the group, setgid bits and default ACLs
  %%> - writes `.env` for `orbit` with group `work`, and the placeholder key, Claude Code and Codex settings for `agent`
  %%> - links `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` of `agent` to the note of the Project type
  %%> - writes `/etc/orbit/instance`, owned by root and readable by all: the Instance, its Project and its URL, which the note points to
  SW->>C: Start T3<br/>systemctl start t3
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - T3 starts for the first time and creates its identity
  %%> - adds the T3 project `/srv/workspace` as `agent`, so a thread can start in it
  %%> Check:
  %%> - waits up to 30 s for `/.well-known/t3/environment`, else `instance.t3_unready`
  SW->>C: Run Project setup steps<br/>Ansible · tags setup
  %%> As whom:
  %%> - each step runs as `orbit` in the workspace, one after another; the first failure stops the run
  %%> When:
  %%> - a Project without setup steps runs no setup phase
  SW->>C: Create, start Processes<br/>child operation-process-create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - each Process is a systemd unit in the container with `User=orbit`
  %%> Why after setup:
  %%> - Processes need the installed dependencies
  opt web-serving Project
    SW->>N: Create the Route<br/>child operation-route-create
    %%> What it adds:
    %%> - the same steps as `route:create`, with its key and signature, then a TLS probe of the site
    %%> - the Node's Caddy proxies the Route to the web Process at the container's bridge address
    %%> - only an Orbit Process is ever a Route target, so a preview reaches only `orbit`
  end
  SW->>C: Issue the Gateway session<br/>sensitive output · vault
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - see container/t3-register.mmd: `t3 auth session issue --label "Orbit Gateway"` as `agent`, stored in the vault
  %%> - the step itself checks the served environment id and the session's scopes; the run returns the environment id, URL and vault key
  alt all steps pass in budget
    C-->>SW: T3 and site answer<br/>Processes running
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record Instance, T3 server<br/>active · registered
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Instance, its runtime and its Route become active
    %%> - the Conn layer records the T3 server from the result and moves its session from the vault; its Node is the container's Node and it names the Instance
  else Instance already created
    Note over GW: Skipped — already created<br/>instance.exists
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Instance is active and its first setup finished, so no step runs
  else a step fails or the budget ends
    C--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    SW->>N: Withdraw the Route<br/>child route-withdraw
    %%> When:
    %%> - only when the run published it
    SW->>N: Stop the container<br/>incus stop
    %%> What stays:
    %%> - the stopped container, its database and its runtime record, marked failed; `instance:destroy` removes them
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    Note over GW: Record the failure
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it resumes on the same container and database
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
